# Campentra — Cursor Rules

## Project Principles
- Keep the code clean, modular, readable, and maintainable.
- Prefer simple, reliable solutions over unnecessary complexity.
- Do not introduce libraries or frameworks unless they are genuinely needed.
- Preserve existing functionality when making changes.
- Before changing architecture, inspect the existing project structure and code.

## Development Workflow
- Work incrementally and make one logical change at a time.
- Reuse existing components, utilities, and styles where appropriate.
- Avoid duplicate code.
- Keep files focused on a single responsibility.
- Clearly handle loading, empty, error, and success states.

## UI / UX
- Keep the interface responsive across mobile, tablet, and desktop.
- Prioritize accessibility and clear user interactions.
- Maintain a consistent visual language throughout Campentra.
- Do not add unnecessary animations or visual effects.

## Code Quality
- Use meaningful names for variables, functions, components, and files.
- Add comments only where they clarify non-obvious logic.
- Handle errors gracefully.
- Do not leave debugging code, temporary logs, or unused imports in production code.

## Security
- Never hard-code API keys, passwords, tokens, or other secrets.
- Keep secrets in environment variables.
- Validate user input where appropriate.
- Do not expose sensitive information in client-side code.

## Git
- Make focused changes.
- Use clear commit messages.
- Do not modify or delete files unrelated to the current task.
